@page "/"

<PageTitle>TraceableAI — Traceable PRISMA Literature Reviews</PageTitle>

<header class="bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex-none shrink-0 z-50 shadow-md">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 h-14 flex items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center space-x-3 hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">
            <span class="font-bold tracking-tight text-sm">AARHUS UNIVERSITY</span>
            <span class="text-white/40 font-light">|</span>
            <span class="text-xs tracking-wider font-medium opacity-90 uppercase">au-btech-literature-review-agent</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto bg-white text-gray-900">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#003B5C] mb-5">
                Aarhus University &middot; Department of Business Development and Technology
            </p>
            <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900">
                TraceableAI
            </h1>
            <p class="font-serif text-xl lg:text-2xl text-gray-700 mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-snug">
                Systematic literature reviews you can check afterwards.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-base text-gray-600 mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
                An open-source agent that runs PRISMA 2020&ndash;compliant literature reviews and keeps a
                record of every step, so every statement in the final report can be traced back to the paper
                it came from.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
                <a href="/review"
                   class="bg-[#003B5C] text-white px-7 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider hover:bg-[#00293f] transition-colors">
                    Get Started
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/lauPhilip/au-btech-literature-review-agent"
                   class="border border-gray-300 text-gray-800 px-7 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider hover:border-[#003B5C] hover:text-[#003B5C] transition-colors">
                    View on GitHub
                </a>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-6">
                Requires a Mistral API key. Free and open source under the Apache 2.0 license.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What it does -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">What it does</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-gray-200 border border-gray-200">
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Claims tied to sources</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Before writing, it maps each point to the papers that support it, then writes against
                        that outline instead of filling in placeholders.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Citations that check out</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Every reference number in the generated text is checked against the actual reference
                        list. Invalid numbers are removed and logged, so nothing is cited that isn&rsquo;t
                        really there.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Searches from several angles</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Each source is queried a few different ways to surface papers a single phrasing would
                        miss, with duplicates removed. You can cap the results per source for quick test runs.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">A complete, downloadable record</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Every run produces a single archive with the report, a log of every screening decision,
                        the source PDFs, and the citation audit.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">How it works</h2>
            <ol class="space-y-6">
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Search</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            Queries academic and open sources &mdash; arXiv, ScienceDirect/Scopus, IEEE Xplore,
                            Google Scholar, and ResearchGate &mdash; using a few phrasings of your query.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Screen</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            Each candidate is checked against your inclusion and exclusion rules, with an
                            optional peer-review-only filter.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">3</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Download</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            The PDFs of the papers that pass are saved into a working folder for the run.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">4</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Read the PDFs</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            The text is extracted page by page and split into short chunks, each tagged with the
                            paper it came from.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">5</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Write the report</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            Those chunks are used to produce the PRISMA checklist items, with the citation check
                            applied to the text.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why traceability -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">Why traceability</h2>
            <div class="border-l-2 border-[#003B5C] pl-6 max-w-3xl">
                <p class="font-serif text-lg lg:text-xl text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
                    Automated review tools tend to produce fluent text with citations that are broken or
                    invented. That makes them hard to trust, and unsuitable for standards like PRISMA 2020,
                    where you are expected to show how you reached your conclusions. TraceableAI is built
                    around keeping that trail intact.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between gap-4">
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
                <span class="font-semibold text-gray-700">TraceableAI</span> &middot; Aarhus University, BTECH<br />
                Presented at OSSYM 2026
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-600">
                <a href="https://github.com/lauPhilip/au-btech-literature-review-agent" class="hover:text-[#003B5C] transition-colors">GitHub</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/lauPhilip/au-btech-literature-review-agent/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md" class="hover:text-[#003B5C] transition-colors">Contributing</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/lauPhilip/au-btech-literature-review-agent/blob/master/LICENSE" class="hover:text-[#003B5C] transition-colors">Apache 2.0 License</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </footer>

</main>
